\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: EUR/USD Likely Well Supported In Asia - \uc2 HSBC\b0\par\par\uc2 1,080 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 23:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2136 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD likely to be well supported in Asian session as fears of European debt crisis fading further into background. But \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  NZ Chief Manager Daniel Brdanovic notes market will have one eye on USD/JPY to see if anything happens there after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; "the market is a little bit wary." EUR/USD last 1.3077 vs 1.3085 late NY, tips support at 1.3035-1.3050, resistance at 1.3150; "Asia will treat it as a buy the dips, so there is still some upside pressure." (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 2115 GMT [Dow Jones] NZ government bonds, IRS unchanged early as market waits for large government bond tender later in day, says local bond trader. Debt Management Office to offer NZ$200 million April 2015s, NZ$75 million December 2017s, NZ$150 million May 2021s. Trader says bonds well bid in recent days, expects tender to go off well. Adds swaps rallied harder than bonds yields yesterday as market waiting for tender; 2-year swap rates unchanged at 3.75%, 10-year swaps unchanged at 4.96%, Nov 2011s yields unchanged at 3.61%. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2029 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  retains year-end target of 0.6800 on NZD/USD, last 0.7244. Says local issues such as recent finance company collapse, rebuilding after Christchurch earthquake should weigh on NZD; "RBNZ is on hold for the near-term, the data flow out of Australia has been superior, and local events such as the collapse of SCF and the earthquake are on balance NZD negative." Tips further NZD under-performance next year as RBA forges away with tightening cycle. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2013 GMT [Dow Jones] Simon Lewis, previously official spokesman for former U.K. Prime Minister Gordon Brown, taking over as chief executive for the Association for Financial Markets in Europe, a lobbying group for the financial services industry. Lewis, who also worked in public relations for \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  and Buckingham Palace, takes over CEO role from Mark Austen, AFME's head of markets policy who will become chief operating officer. Lewis takes the job Oct. 1. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2010 GMT [Dow Jones] The New York Fed's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program remains lightly utilized. The ECB rolled over the $60 million it drew a week ago, and the Bank of Japan saw $3 million of the $4 million it borrowed maturing, leaving total outstanding at $61 million. Demand for dollar liquidity among the world's major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be without problems, hence the minimal activity. (michael.derby@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2004 GMT [Dow Jones] Asset-backed securities valued at $74.87B have been sold versus $104.5B last year this time, according to Citi data. Auto sector issuance comprises 55% of the total, at $41.21B. Last year by this time, it was about 40% of total at $41.87B. The auto sector of the asset-backed market has come to life this week. \uc2 Nissan Motor\uc2  sold a $1.3B bond, \uc2 BMW\uc2  sold a $1B security and \uc2 AmeriCredit\uc2  Auto Receivables Trust priced a $850M bond. There was robust demand for all these new bonds and most were increased in size.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2004 GMT [Dow Jones] Hedging from corporate and agency bond sales take down long-term Tsy futures prices. Also, competition from the offerings weigh on contracts tied to lower-yielding Tsys. Dec 10-yr Tsy notes settled down 9/32 at 123-29, near 2.75% cash yield equivalent. Dec 30-yr Tsy bonds settled 25/32 lower at 129-28. Dec ultra long Tsy bonds settled at 135-31, down 31/32. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2001 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wrap: The euro climbed to its strongest level against the dollar in more than a month on the heels of a well-received auction of Spanish government debt and amid speculation the U.S. will initiate another round of economy-stimulating asset purchases. The dollar, meanwhile, held onto its sharp gains against the yen a day after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strangle the recent strength in the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . China's yuan rose to the strongest level since it began trading in 1994, the fourth consecutive session in which the yuan hit a record intraday high, on a day when Tsy Sec Geithner said in Congressional testimony China's move toward a more flexible exchange rate has been "too slow."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (bradley.davis@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2000 GMT [Dow Jones] Lingering worries about a slowing economy provided enough ammunition for fed-funds futures traders to continue paring bets for 3Q 2011 rate increase. Oct '11 prices in 40% chance for FOMC to raise funds rate to 0.5% at next Sept's meeting. That's down from 46% chance Tues and Wed, 62% chance Mon and 76% chance last Fri. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2000 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD likely to have quieter session as market digests events of week, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Pair last 0.7247 versus 0.7244 late yesterday after subdued statement from RBNZ; "We expected an on-hold decision, and a more relaxed tone, but we were surprised by the extent that the RBNZ lowered its projections for the 90 day bill rate." Says topside moves, if attempted, likely limited to 0.7274 while support around 0.7200 should be enough to provide base. Notes strengthening EUR, AUD should help negate attempts to move lower at this point. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1957 GMT [Dow Jones] Canadian bonds end lower, taking direction from U.S. Treasurys in the absence of any significant domestic data or other market-moving events on the local front. The two-year bond is at 1.511% late vs 1.480% late Wed. The 10-year bond yields 2.976% vs 2.963%. There are no significant Canadian data releases Fri, but the calendar quickens next week, with Aug CPI data on Tues. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1955 GMT[Dow Jones] The yields are out on $2B Ukraine bonds. The $500M 5-year tranche will yield 6.875%, while the $1.5B 10-year tranche will yield 7.75%. Final pricing with coupon value is expected later Thu. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com) [ 09-16-10 1736ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g000ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
