\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Yen Stays Down Post- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Euro Gains Vs. Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 762 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 22:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar held onto its sharp gains against the yen a day after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strangle the recent strength in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's estimated Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has left \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors cautious, with Japanese officials saying more action could be on the table to stem the yen's strength, a stance that might have also given a boost to the euro, said Steven Englander, head of G10 strategy at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "If the market becomes convinced that [Japan] will be resisting U.S. dollar weakness against the yen, other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become more attractive as U.S. dollar alternatives," he said.\par \par \uc2 After Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's biggest daily yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Prime Minister Naoto Kan reiterated Thursday that the country will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when necessary.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the euro was at $1.3085, up from $1.3012 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG, off its intraday high of $1.3117, but still up more than 0.5% on the day. The dollar was at Y85.81, up from Y85.63, while the euro was at Y112.29, up from Y111.36. The U.K. pound was at $1.5635, up from $1.5623. The dollar was at CHF1.0146, up from CHF1.0035.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 81.224, down from 81.453.\par \par \uc2 To see the dollar's performance against the yen, please see:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4604"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4604}}}\par \par \uc2 The euro Thursday climbed to its strongest level against the dollar in more than a month on the heels of a well-received auction of Spanish government debt that helped the region's debt crisis fade further into the background. The debt sale followed successful auctions earlier this week in Italy and Greece.\par \par \uc2 Investors may also see the euro as a sensible temporary safety play, said Alan Ruskin, global head of G-10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  in New York, as concerns mount that the Federal Reserve will implement a fresh round of asset purchases, known as quantitative easing, to jolt a slowing economy. Further loosened monetary policy would weigh on the greenback, with investors using cheap dollars to fund bets on higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With investors also cautious about any further moves by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper yen strength after Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro might offer the best opportunity to express antidollar sentiment, Ruskin said.\par \par \uc2 But "long-term sentiment toward the euro is still very negative," Ruskin said, with the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely to muster a gain beyond $1.35.\par \par \uc2 The euro, along with the dollar, also shot higher against the Swiss franc, each gaining more than 1%, after the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  Thursday left key interest rates unchanged, noting weakening inflation and a slowdown in growth for the rest of 2010 and in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner said in Congressional testimony Thursday that China's move toward a more flexible exchange rate has been "too slow," though Geithner signalled the Obama administration was reluctant to formally label China a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator under U.S. law. China's yuan rose overnight to its strongest level since it began trading in 1994, the fourth consecutive session in which the yuan hit a record intraday high.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Russian ruble extended losses Thursday to close at its lowest levels since February, with analysts expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brazilian Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  said his country also was ready with a dollar-buying strategy to curb unwanted appreciation of the Brazilian real, which has gained strongly against the greenback recently on an inflow of dollars from overseas bond placements by Brazilian companies and on global investor interest in the planned offer of Brazilian oil giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With the ICE Dollar Index weakening, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bearish exchange-traded fund was up 0.27% from late Wednesday, while its PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bullish was down 0.34%. The two exchange-traded funds are based on \uc2 Deutsche Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures indexes, whose composition mirrors that of the ICE's Dollar Index.\par \par \uc2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654; bradley.davis@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Andrew J. Johnson in New York contributed to this article.) [ 09-16-10 1614ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g000dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
