\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Euro-Zone's Juncker Speaks Against  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,103 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 18:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1616 GMT [Dow Jones] Luxembourg PM Jean-Claude Juncker hit out Thu at Japanese action on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to prop up the yen, saying his euro zone partners "don't like unilateral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." USD/JPY holding its strong gains from massive Wed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , almost frozen at 85.72 from 85.63 late Wed, according to EBS via CQG. (bradley.davis@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1605 GMT [Dow Jones] CAD continues to perform remarkably well even though commodity prices have stumbled during the past couple of days, the domestic economic data have softened substantially and the money markets are starting to price out more interest rate action out of the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 , says David Rosenberg, chief economist and strategist at Gluskin/Sheff in Toronto. "When we talk to global investors about what it is they want in their portfolios, it is mostly oil, gold and food. Although, these comprise 40% of the Canadian equity market, they are barely more than 10% in the U.S.A.," he says. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1558 GMT [Dow Jones] The long bond is under heavy pressure, its yield recently hit 3.959%, the highest level since 3.964% on Aug. 13. The yield is now up about 7BP to 3.946%.\par \par \uc2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1550 GMT [Dow Jones] SNB's Hildebrand Thu declined to say whether the SNB may resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken CHF, but said it has a clear mandate to ensure price stability. In an interview with Swiss national radio, Hildebrand said: "We must also consider the economic situation." \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier Thu left key rates unchanged, noting weakening inflation and slowing economy. USD and EUR up sharply vs. CHF, both notching more than 1% gains.\par \par \uc2 (bradley.davis@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1540 GMT [Dow Jones] Harrisburg, Pa is grappling with $288M in debt tied to an incinerator project -- over four times its annual budget-- as well as a $4.5M budget gap. A city councilman wants to hire a attorney to explore a Chapter 9 muni bankruptcy filing, which is opposed by the mayor. "Depending how this small case turns out, other cities in the same boat could follow its lead," says Marilyn Cohen of Envision Capital in a note. "Should the strategy of bankruptcy allow Harrisburg to find a way out, we will likely see a spate of municipal bankruptcies." (romy.varghese@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1535 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungarian government bond prices fall after sufficient but not outstanding buying activity at the 12-month treasury bill auction. Bond yields are up slightly; the 3-year benchmark yield is at 6.86%, 5-year is also 6.86%, and 10-year at 6.90%. Yields are seen trading sideways in short term after a rally in the past few days on the Hungarian government's commitment to a budget deficit target of below 3% of GDP in 2011. EUR/HUF is 282.69 from 281.80 in the morning, and CHF/HUF is 212.98 after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hold decision from 216.65 in the morning. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1519 GMT [Dow Jones] Fed buys $1.379 billion in three short-dated Treasurys notes on over $30B in offers. The small size of buying fails to give Treasurys a lift, which is pressured mainly by hedge-selling related to new corporate and agency debt supply. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1510 GMT [Dow Jones] All Treasurys fall, despite Fed buying in short end, but long issues are bearing the brunt of selling as companies hedge new debt supply. Among the notable issues is the \uc2 Tennessee Valley Authority\uc2  (TVA), a federally chartered company, which is in the market with 50-year debt expected to be $500 million and price later today. 10-year note's price is 13/32 lower to yield 2.770%. The 30-year bond is 1 pt lower to yield 3.939%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1458 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY holding gains and steady at 85.71, from 85.63 late Wed. While China's policy facing increasing scrutiny from US officials, Geithner testimony unlikely to lead to any immediate real wide swings in USD/JPY or cease \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, said Steven Barrow, head of G10 strategy at Standard Bank in London. "Stealing competitiveness from your peers can't be well-received from Geithner and others," said Barrow. "That said, it likely won't change anything with the dollar-yen," short-term, because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already been taken, and what is done is done, Barrow said. Geithner's comments are unlikely to deter \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because it has already acted once and will follow through on its own strategy, he said. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1455 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CAD has been caught in a choppy range trade since the beginning of summer, but the break out could be violent when it finally comes. "At some point, likely late this year or early next, USD/CAD will find the catalyst sufficiently strong enough to push it to a new level," says Scotia Capital. "Historically, when USD/CAD has broken out of its range, it has been a rapid, violent and sustained break, which catches most by surprise, Scotia adds. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1452 GMT [Dow Jones] Much of the agency debt market participants are on a quest this morning to find out more details about a bond, specifically a 50-year issue from the \uc2 Tennessee Valley Authority\uc2 , which is a GSE. However, information is scarce, and book-runners \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  have put out little. Talk is that the issue, expected to be of size $500 million, is created for investors who already have put their names down. (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1447 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish bonds yields are stable after a strong primary auction of 10-year bonds in Poland on Wednesday and a EUR1 billion eurobond issue on Thursday, with both issues strongly oversubscribed, a trader says. Adds yields are expected lower in the longer term, particularly for longer maturities. Average yield of 2-year bonds is flat from Wednesday afternoon at 4.63%, 5-year flat at 5.10%, 10-year at 5.45% from 5.46%. EUR/PLN is at 3.9467 from 3.9357, USD/PLN at 3.0144 from 3.0258. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com) [ 09-16-10 1216ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g000c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
