\par\par \b \uc2 Long-Dated Treasurys Lower In Choppy Trade After Jobs Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Min Zeng   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 15:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Long-dated Treasurys fell Thursday, with the 30-year bond the biggest loser, hurt by concern about further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame the yen's gains.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year and 30-year maturities fell a day earlier as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in six years spurred many investors to shift money into short-dated notes that are believed to be Japan's favored places to park its dollar proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Hedge selling from companies issuing new corporate debt also weighed, as did an unexpected decline in the jobless claims that offered some optimism about the labor market. By selling Treasurys, they can neutralize the risks of higher interest rates, making the debt sales more cost-effective.\par \par \uc2 "There are so many cross currents" and Treasurys are "the whipping post," says Thomas Roth at Mitsubishi UFJ Securities (USA). "We are the hedge for all markets and get whipped back and forth as those hedges are put on and taken off."\par \par \uc2 As of 9:30 a.m. EDT, the benchmark 10-year Treasury note was down 6/32 in price and its yield was up to 2.744%. The 30-year bond was down 24/32 to yield 3.918%. Bond yields move inversely to prices.\par \par \uc2 Shorter-dated Treasurys suffered the least in a volatile session, especially the three-year and five-year notes, as they got support from the Federal Reserve. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is scheduled to buy Treasurys targeting maturities in two years to three years at 10:30 a.m. EDT.\par \par \uc2 Initial unemployment claims declined by 3,000 to 450,000 in the week ended Sept. 11, the Labor Department said in its weekly report Thursday. New claims for the previous week, ended Sept. 4, were revised upward slightly to 453,000 from 451,000. Economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires had expected new claims would rise by 9,000.\par \par \uc2 The index of producer prices, which measures how much manufacturers and wholesalers pay for goods and materials, rose a seasonally-adjusted 0.4% for finished goods in August from July, a Labor Department report showed Thursday. In July, wholesale prices were up 0.2%. The figures were exactly in line with a survey of economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 -By Min Zeng, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2229; min.zeng@dowjones.com [ 09-16-10 0940ET ]\par \par \uc2 1079 20715 4041   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g0009s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
