\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: India IRS Curve Flattening Limited - BarCap\b0\par\par\uc2 1,210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 10:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0830 GMT [Dow Jones] As India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indicates policy rates close to "normal levels", RBI may refrain from hiking rates for rest of year, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 . This means further increases in short-end rates may be capped, limiting further curve flattening move, house adds. Recommends exit of previous 2x5 OIS flattener trade. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0828 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR tad higher at 8,985 vs 8,975 late yesterday in sluggish trade; players covering short positions on concerns regional central banks could follow in footsteps of Japan, weaken their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers say. "I think players are very cautious and they are wondering what BOJ will do (next) and how other central banks will react," dealer says; 8,970-8,995 range tipped for Friday. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0827 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CHF will "collapse" should the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  defy market expectations and raise interest rates later Thursday, according to \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . "Markets are pricing in a 5% chance of an SNB increase, and while the strong economy may warrant a hike, it may be reluctant to hike given the CHF strength," say analysts. "We remain bearish EUR/CHF overall and hence would use EUR/CHF moves towards 1.3070 to establish short positions," they add. EUR/CHF at 1.3029. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0826 GMT [Dow Jones] A \uc2 Hochtief\uc2  (HOT.XE) takeover by ACS (ACS.MC) would make strategic sense, says \uc2 Bankhaus Lampe\uc2  analyst Marc Gabriel. Regionally the two companies have little overlap and acquisition of \uc2 Hochtief\uc2  would shoot ACS into global player position. Gabriel says until now \uc2 Hochtief\uc2 's share price hasn't accounted for its stake in Leighton, which alone would be worth EUR60 per share, excluding \uc2 Hochtief\uc2 's own \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Buy rating on \uc2 Hochtief\uc2  EUR71 target. ACS and \uc2 Hochtief\uc2  have declined to comment. \uc2 Hochtief\uc2  shares 7.5% at EUR60.55, ACS shares suspended having last traded at EUR34.80. (thomas.leppert@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] The JPY has been pushed marginally higher again now that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A warning from a US Senator that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "deeply disturbing" has raised fears that Treasury Secretary Geithner will criticize the move when he speaks later in the day. This could damage the outlook for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The USD is down at Y85.48 while the EUR has slipped to Y111.29. The EUR is up at $1.3021 while the GBP is marginally lower at $1.5619 as it waits for the latest UK retail sales data. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0817 GMT [Dow Jones] Sweden's unemployment level of 7.4% in August, down from 8% in July, was much lower than both Handelsbanken and consensus expectations, Handelsbanken says. "The reason for the large downturn was primarily very weak growth in the labor force," the bank says. Employment growth at 1.6% on the year was weaker than Handelsbanken had expected but should pick up in the future, the bank adds. (charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0813 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CHF is hovering just over 1.30 as it waits for the SNB to confirm that it is leaving rates unchanged. But, says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 , the pair could fall under 1.30 again if the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stresses the medium term risks of inflation and signals that rate rises are on their way. The pair is now at 1.3032. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty is up in tandem with the euro's strengthening vs the dollar, a dealer says. The EUR/PLN is seen being stuck in its range from the past couple of days, 3.9200-3.9550, a dealer says. EUR/PLN trades at 3.9381 from 3.9412 late Wednesday; USD/PLN at 3.0247 from 3.0345. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.62% from 4.65% late Wednesday, on 5-year at 5.10% from 5.11%, on 10-year at 5.45% from 5.46%. (marynia.kruk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR implied volatilities higher; gamma finally finds takers as spot pair falls after RBI raised its key borrowing rate by more-than-expected 50 bps, says trader with foreign bank; 1-month ATMF at 6.50%/7.20% vs 6.20%/6.80% late Wednesday. But options market not wholly convinced on sustainable spot correction--risk reversals haven't met further selling today, while back-end volatilities also largely unchanged, says trader. "I'd say people are trying to make money on a knee-jerk reaction, without assuming a further correction beyond the next week or two," says trader. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0808 GMT [Dow Jones] With the market leaving the JPY alone due to fears of provoking BOJ action, the Swiss franc on the sidelines ahead of the SNB's rate decision at 1200 GMT and the euro is constrained by strong resistance around $1.3035 sterling may be the only play ahead of the US open. UK retail sales are out at 0830 GMT and anything above the 0.3% consensus could propel GBP/USD toward 1.57 says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  while \uc2 Lloyds Banking Group\uc2  says any disappointment from the number combined with a weak Philly Fed survey this afternoon could trigger profit taking toward the 1.55 area. GBP/USD currently trades at 1.5605. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0807 GMT [Dow Jones] Swedish unemployment data in August confirms the jobless rate is trending lower, falling to 7.4% from 8% in July against SEB's forecasts for 7.9%, the bank notes. "Labor market indicators remain firm and the upward trend in employment since the middle of last year will probably accelerate going into 2011," SEB says. "Swedish data continue to indicate upwards pressure on the Rikbank's repo rate path," it adds. EUR/SEK trades at 9.2126.(ian.edmondson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0801 GMT [Dow Jones] iTraxx Japanese Series 13 indicated at 96.5/97.5 bps vs yesterday's close of 98 bps; but index wasn't actually traded ahead of benchmark contract's rollover next week, says Japan bank trader. USD-denominated CDS spreads on Japanese sovereign debt done at 65 bps vs 78 bps on August 26, 4-year protection at 51, 50, 49 bps vs yesterday's 50 bps; Japanese sovereign CDS through Dec. 2015 at 69.5 bps. Other single-name CDS deals include \uc2 Toyota Motor Corp\uc2 . (7203.TO) at 55 bps vs 64 bps on Sept. 6, \uc2 Mitsubishi Estate Co. Ltd\uc2 . (8802.TO) at 52 bps vs 60 bps on July 6, \uc2 Nippon Steel Corp\uc2 . (5401.TO) at 51 bps vs 54 bps on July 30, \uc2 Hankyu Hanshin Holdings Inc\uc2 . (9042.TO) at 65 bps, \uc2 Kajima Corp\uc2 . (1812.TO) at 190 bps vs 195 bps on August 3, 3-year at 100 bps vs 120 bps on August 10, \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2  USD-subordinated CDS at 110 bps vs 130 bps on Sept. 2, USD-senior at 70 bps. (megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com) [ 09-16-10 0430ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g00061\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
