8.12 off earlier low of CNY8.07, \uc2 Poly Real Estate Group\uc2  (600048.SH) down 0.3% at CNY11.12 off earlier low of 11.07. Shenzhen Composite Index down 2.4% at 1153.66. (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0417 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY could fall below 85.00 by end of global day, as apparent absence of any Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves pair prone to selling by Japanese exporters, other players taking profits, says senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at major Japanese bank. After U.S. Congressman Levin, chair of House Ways and Means Committee, said overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "deeply disturbing," trader says any more negative comments from U.S. officials would weigh further on pair. Investors will closely watch U.S. Treasury Secretary Geithner testimony before Senate committee at 1400 GMT, before House committee at 1800 GMT for any cues to thinking on Japan move. But dealer says most likely, Geithner will refrain from direct comment on Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF has likely received Treasury's assurance to refrain from direct criticism of Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/JPY last at 85.28. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0414 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds tad down as markets await \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-quarter policy announcement, says dealer with private bank; 7.80% 2020 benchmark bond at 99.00 vs 99.02 Wednesday close. "The next move in the market will be only after the policy. However, a 25 basis point hike is already factored in and may not lead to a major fall," says dealer. Adds, "the market will closely watch the tone of the policy. If a rate hike is accompanied by a hawkish statement, we may see a big fall in bond prices." Tips yield on 10-year paper in tight range of 7.94%-7.96%, last at 7.95%. Notes, yields may fall to 7.80% if RBI keeps both rates unchanged. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei down 0.1% at 9507.27, turning negative after positive morning performance as USD/JPY weakens (now 85.26). Futures selling dragging down cash market, says Hikaru Sato, senior technical analyst at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets. "Investors want more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but there is a sense of disillusionment that the government may not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," he says. Analysts say if USD/JPY falls below 85, Nikkei may be supported at 9450, while if pair stays above 85 exporters may keep gains. \uc2 Mazda\uc2  (7261.TO) up 0.5% at Y202, \uc2 Sony\uc2  (6758.TO) up 1.5% at Y2,637. Commodity stocks lower; Inpex (1605.TO) down 2.2% at Y402,500 on falling crude prices. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  great tailwind for JGBs if BOJ leaves \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilized, which is what investors are anticipating, says Tetsuya Miura, chief market analyst at Mizuho Securities. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shifted the BOJ's policy direction to further policy easing. That said, the bond market is probably the one which benefits the most from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he says. Adds benchmark 10-year yield could fall well below 1.10% again vs last 1.050%, up 1 bps. Lead December futures last at 142.17, up 0.05. BOJ injects Y1 trillion into money market at 0400 GMT, sign that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may leave some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds in markets. (takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0403 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex up 0.2% at 19,535.99, rebounds after opening 0.2% lower, hit 19,456.71 in early trade; but remains rangebound as investors tread cautiously ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate decision due 0630 GMT. 18 index issues up, 12 down, with SBI (500112.BY) +2.3% at INR3,132.80 helped by report bank in talks with RBI about forming holding company that will control equity of bank, its associates and units. \uc2 Infosys (500209.BY) \uc2 down 1.8% at INR2,994 on profit-booking. "Its a subdued start as traders reluctant to take a call before the RBI rate-setting meeting decision. Select banks are witnessing some buying interest on positive newsflow," says local fund manager. Says, the markets have discounted a 25 bps hike each in repo rate, reverse repo rate. Tips Sensex in 19,450-19,580 range until rate decision. \uc2 Hero Honda Motors\uc2  (500182.BY) +1.5% at INR1,764, ONGC (500312.BY) +1.2% at INR1,427.95. But, TCS (532540.BY) down 1.2% at INR902.55, \uc2 Mahindra & Mahindra\uc2  (500520.BY) off 1% at INR669.90. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0402 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares last +0.2% at 449.57 on hopes government will soon come up with measures to help improve liquidity conditions; government said last week it will act to stabilize stock market. Still concerns over equity dilution remain after brokerage analysts said recently banks, companies expected to issue large amounts of new shares between now and year-end. Volume thin with 23.3 million shares valued at VND620 billion traded so far. Trader tips resistance at 450. Among advancers, \uc2 Bao Viet Holdings\uc2  (BVH.VH) last +0.6% at VND48,700, \uc2 PetroVietnam\uc2  Drilling (PVD.VH) +0.4% at VND43,700, \uc2 Hoa Phat Group\uc2  (HPG.VH) +0.8% at VND38,200. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0354 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR tad up as equity markets flat, says dealer with private bank; pair at 46.39 vs 46.36 in late Wednesday trade. "Markets are awaiting the RBI policy announcement. A rate hike could lead INR to appreciate as it will widen the interest rate differential between India and U.S. and attract more debt flows," says dealer. Tips pair to be in 46.35-46.45 range till policy release. Notes, pair may find support at 46.28 if RBI hikes rates. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0354 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP moving higher, with banks watching out for possible JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities; pair last at 44.35 after holding steady at 44.26 late Wednesday; support 44.00, resistance 44.50; "We're still moving in a narrow range, waiting for what will happen to the yen. Local stocks are up, so that's providing some support to the peso," says local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com) [ 09-16-10 0034ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g0002y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
