er, a 25 basis point hike is already factored in and may not lead to a major fall," says dealer. Adds, "the market will closely watch the tone of the policy. If a rate hike is accompanied by a hawkish statement, we may see a big fall in bond prices." Tips yield on 10-year paper in tight range of 7.94%-7.96%, last at 7.95%. Notes, yields may fall to 7.80% if RBI keeps both rates unchanged. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei down 0.1% at 9507.27, turning negative after positive morning performance as USD/JPY weakens (now 85.26). Futures selling dragging down cash market, says Hikaru Sato, senior technical analyst at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets. "Investors want more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but there is a sense of disillusionment that the government may not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," he says. Analysts say if USD/JPY falls below 85, Nikkei may be supported at 9450, while if pair stays above 85 exporters may keep gains. \uc2 Mazda\uc2  (7261.TO) up 0.5% at Y202, \uc2 Sony\uc2  (6758.TO) up 1.5% at Y2,637. Commodity stocks lower; Inpex (1605.TO) down 2.2% at Y402,500 on falling crude prices. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  great tailwind for JGBs if BOJ leaves \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilized, which is what investors are anticipating, says Tetsuya Miura, chief market analyst at Mizuho Securities. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shifted the BOJ's policy direction to further policy easing. That said, the bond market is probably the one which benefits the most from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he says. Adds benchmark 10-year yield could fall well below 1.10% again vs last 1.050%, up 1 bps. Lead December futures last at 142.17, up 0.05. BOJ injects Y1 trillion into money market at 0400 GMT, sign that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may leave some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds in markets. (takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0403 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex up 0.2% at 19,535.99, rebounds after opening 0.2% lower, hit 19,456.71 in early trade; but remains rangebound as investors tread cautiously ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate decision due 0630 GMT. 18 index issues up, 12 down, with SBI (500112.BY) +2.3% at INR3,132.80 helped by report bank in talks with RBI about forming holding company that will control equity of bank, its associates and units. \uc2 Infosys (500209.BY) \uc2 down 1.8% at INR2,994 on profit-booking. "Its a subdued start as traders reluctant to take a call before the RBI rate-setting meeting decision. Select banks are witnessing some buying interest on positive newsflow," says local fund manager. Says, the markets have discounted a 25 bps hike each in repo rate, reverse repo rate. Tips Sensex in 19,450-19,580 range until rate decision. \uc2 Hero Honda Motors\uc2  (500182.BY) +1.5% at INR1,764, ONGC (500312.BY) +1.2% at INR1,427.95. But, TCS (532540.BY) down 1.2% at INR902.55, \uc2 Mahindra & Mahindra\uc2  (500520.BY) off 1% at INR669.90. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0402 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares last +0.2% at 449.57 on hopes government will soon come up with measures to help improve liquidity conditions; government said last week it will act to stabilize stock market. Still concerns over equity dilution remain after brokerage analysts said recently banks, companies expected to issue large amounts of new shares between now and year-end. Volume thin with 23.3 million shares valued at VND620 billion traded so far. Trader tips resistance at 450. Among advancers, \uc2 Bao Viet Holdings\uc2  (BVH.VH) last +0.6% at VND48,700, \uc2 PetroVietnam\uc2  Drilling (PVD.VH) +0.4% at VND43,700, \uc2 Hoa Phat Group\uc2  (HPG.VH) +0.8% at VND38,200. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0354 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR tad up as equity markets flat, says dealer with private bank; pair at 46.39 vs 46.36 in late Wednesday trade. "Markets are awaiting the RBI policy announcement. A rate hike could lead INR to appreciate as it will widen the interest rate differential between India and U.S. and attract more debt flows," says dealer. Tips pair to be in 46.35-46.45 range till policy release. Notes, pair may find support at 46.28 if RBI hikes rates. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0354 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP moving higher, with banks watching out for possible JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities; pair last at 44.35 after holding steady at 44.26 late Wednesday; support 44.00, resistance 44.50; "We're still moving in a narrow range, waiting for what will happen to the yen. Local stocks are up, so that's providing some support to the peso," says local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0349 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/JPY falls to 110.65 as Japan exporters' EUR sales triggered stop loss orders below 111.00, says senior dealer at major Japan trust bank. USD/JPY falls to 85.26, EUR/USD to 1.2975 in tandem. Says support for EUR/JPY up to how far dollar/yen falls, with USD/JPY being closely watched by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities who may embark on another JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealer declines to guess what level \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at, but notes 85.00 may be key. Aside from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market's focus on exporter USD, EUR sales. EUR/JPY last 85.27, EUR/JPY last 110.75, EUR/USD last 1.2989.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0335 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares trade lower with banks leading declines amid growing concerns about possibility of PBOC interest rate hike, further tightening measures. Agricultural Bank of China (601288.SH) is sector's biggest loser; stock last down 2.2% at CNY2.62, falling below CNY2.68 IPO price for first time. Shanghai Composite Index down 1.8% at 2603.76, tipped to test immediate support at 2600, with 2550 as next target. "The rate hike worries seem to be gathering momentum the longer PBOC maintains its silence," says Li Xin at China Development Bank Securities. "At this point, if PBOC unveils a rate hike, it might actually have a positive effect on the market." \uc2 China Construction Bank\uc2  down 2.0% at CNY4.52. Shenzhen Composite Index down 2.4% at 1153.66. (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0334 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares +0.2% at 923.21 after BOT governor Wednesday says there are no immediate plan to impose measures to curb THB's rise; such worries had put SET index under pressure in past few days as THB weakness would deter foreign investment in market. Weakness in regional bourses likely capped gains, says analyst with Finansia Syrus Securities Somchai Anektaweepon. "Capital inflows are expected to continue flooding into Asian markets including Thailand, so the Thai stock market will tend to go up," he adds. Investors watching if court will issue injunction to block 3G license auction set to kick off next week. Resistance tipped at 925-926, support at 915-910. Among top actives, Land & Houses (LH.TH) +3.8% at THB6.80, Banpu (BANPU.TH) +0.3% at THB644, PTT (PTT.TH) 0.4% at THB282, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) flat at tHB92.50, CP All (CPALL.TH) +2.6% at THB39. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0327 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds mixed in mild trade, with many players holding off as they wait for fresh cues. Participants still skeptical over potential imposition of measures to stem THB strength despite BOT Governor's comment yesterday bank has no immediate plan to take additional steps to curb THB's rise. Such worries pushed up yields in recent sessions. "Most players are waiting to see a clearer picture to be sure that such measures really are not underway," says trader. Yields expected to move within 5 bps range either way today. Bid/offer yields of issue due December 2015 quoted at 2.74%/2.68% vs 2.78%/2.72% late yesterday, November 2016 quoted at 2.87%/2.80% vs 2.90%/2.80%, June 2019 quoted at 3.05%/2.95% vs 2.98%/2.92%. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com) [ 09-16-10 0017ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
