s associates and units. \uc2 Infosys (500209.BY) \uc2 down 1.8% at INR2,994 on profit-booking. "Its a subdued start as traders reluctant to take a call before the RBI rate-setting meeting decision. Select banks are witnessing some buying interest on positive newsflow," says local fund manager. Says, the markets have discounted a 25 bps hike each in repo rate, reverse repo rate. Tips Sensex in 19,450-19,580 range until rate decision. \uc2 Hero Honda Motors\uc2  (500182.BY) +1.5% at INR1,764, ONGC (500312.BY) +1.2% at INR1,427.95. But, TCS (532540.BY) down 1.2% at INR902.55, \uc2 Mahindra & Mahindra\uc2  (500520.BY) off 1% at INR669.90. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0402 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares last +0.2% at 449.57 on hopes government will soon come up with measures to help improve liquidity conditions; government said last week it will act to stabilize stock market. Still concerns over equity dilution remain after brokerage analysts said recently banks, companies expected to issue large amounts of new shares between now and year-end. Volume thin with 23.3 million shares valued at VND620 billion traded so far. Trader tips resistance at 450. Among advancers, \uc2 Bao Viet Holdings\uc2  (BVH.VH) last +0.6% at VND48,700, \uc2 PetroVietnam\uc2  Drilling (PVD.VH) +0.4% at VND43,700, \uc2 Hoa Phat Group\uc2  (HPG.VH) +0.8% at VND38,200. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0354 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR tad up as equity markets flat, says dealer with private bank; pair at 46.39 vs 46.36 in late Wednesday trade. "Markets are awaiting the RBI policy announcement. A rate hike could lead INR to appreciate as it will widen the interest rate differential between India and U.S. and attract more debt flows," says dealer. Tips pair to be in 46.35-46.45 range till policy release. Notes, pair may find support at 46.28 if RBI hikes rates. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0354 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP moving higher, with banks watching out for possible JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities; pair last at 44.35 after holding steady at 44.26 late Wednesday; support 44.00, resistance 44.50; "We're still moving in a narrow range, waiting for what will happen to the yen. Local stocks are up, so that's providing some support to the peso," says local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0349 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/JPY falls to 110.65 as Japan exporters' EUR sales triggered stop loss orders below 111.00, says senior dealer at major Japan trust bank. USD/JPY falls to 85.26, EUR/USD to 1.2975 in tandem. Says support for EUR/JPY up to how far dollar/yen falls, with USD/JPY being closely watched by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities who may embark on another JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealer declines to guess what level \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at, but notes 85.00 may be key. Aside from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market's focus on exporter USD, EUR sales. EUR/JPY last 85.27, EUR/JPY last 110.75, EUR/USD last 1.2989.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0335 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares trade lower with banks leading declines amid growing concerns about possibility of PBOC interest rate hike, further tightening measures. Agricultural Bank of China (601288.SH) is sector's biggest loser; stock last down 2.2% at CNY2.62, falling below CNY2.68 IPO price for first time. Shanghai Composite Index down 1.8% at 2603.76, tipped to test immediate support at 2600, with 2550 as next target. "The rate hike worries seem to be gathering momentum the longer PBOC maintains its silence," says Li Xin at China Development Bank Securities. "At this point, if PBOC unveils a rate hike, it might actually have a positive effect on the market." \uc2 China Construction Bank\uc2  down 2.0% at CNY4.52. Shenzhen Composite Index down 2.4% at 1153.66. (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0334 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares +0.2% at 923.21 after BOT governor Wednesday says there are no immediate plan to impose measures to curb THB's rise; such worries had put SET index under pressure in past few days as THB weakness would deter foreign investment in market. Weakness in regional bourses likely capped gains, says analyst with Finansia Syrus Securities Somchai Anektaweepon. "Capital inflows are expected to continue flooding into Asian markets including Thailand, so the Thai stock market will tend to go up," he adds. Investors watching if court will issue injunction to block 3G license auction set to kick off next week. Resistance tipped at 925-926, support at 915-910. Among top actives, Land & Houses (LH.TH) +3.8% at THB6.80, Banpu (BANPU.TH) +0.3% at THB644, PTT (PTT.TH) 0.4% at THB282, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) flat at tHB92.50, CP All (CPALL.TH) +2.6% at THB39. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0327 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds mixed in mild trade, with many players holding off as they wait for fresh cues. Participants still skeptical over potential imposition of measures to stem THB strength despite BOT Governor's comment yesterday bank has no immediate plan to take additional steps to curb THB's rise. Such worries pushed up yields in recent sessions. "Most players are waiting to see a clearer picture to be sure that such measures really are not underway," says trader. Yields expected to move within 5 bps range either way today. Bid/offer yields of issue due December 2015 quoted at 2.74%/2.68% vs 2.78%/2.72% late yesterday, November 2016 quoted at 2.87%/2.80% vs 2.90%/2.80%, June 2019 quoted at 3.05%/2.95% vs 2.98%/2.92%. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0327 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by 1-month ATM USD/JPY options drop sharply to 11.10%/11.70% vs 11.80%/12.50% New York Wednesday, as spot floats around 85.50 in Asia morning without sharp moves, reducing demand for hedges against fluctuations, such as those on Wednesday when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets. Options dealer at major \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank says view growing that Japan authorities will continue to trim recent JPY strength, further reducing demand for hedging against pair's falls. Dealer says if spot stays around current 85.40-85.50 levels in global day, vols may decline 20 bps; if spot rise gradually, vols may decline toward 10.5% in near term. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0324 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY now at 85.27, may fall below 85.00 due to USD, EUR sales by Japanese exporters if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities do not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market, says Masafumi Yamamoto, Barclays Bank Chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But notes that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever they see opportunity to take market by surprise and will not wait for yen to hit fixed levels to prevent JPY strengthening. Markets focused on whether or not BOJ will continue to leave funds in market instead of "sterilizing" through money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  as is usually done. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from any draining of funds in morning \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  window. Focus now on 0400 GMT money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Leaving funds would effectively add to monetary base and further monetary easing. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0322 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares down 0.4% at 3344.230 with losses in heavyweight \uc2 Astra International\uc2  (ASII.JK) weighing on main index, dealers say; market breadth positive though with gainers leading decliners 69 to 62. Volume healthy with 854 billion shares worth IDR1.1 trillion exchanging hands. "Investors are still buying stocks, but they are selective in their investments after strong gains yesterday," dealer says. Astra down 2.8% at IDR56,250, while its CPO unit Astra Agro (ALLI.JK) down 1.4% at IDR20,650; cigarette maker Gudan Garam (GGRM.JK) down 2.3% at IDR4,500; Telkom (TLKM.JK) +0.5% at IDR9,300. 3,270-3,390 range tipped for main index today. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com) [ 09-16-10 0009ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g0002n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
