\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: JPY Bulls Should Hang On\b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 09:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0721 GMT [Dow Jones] Desperate times call for desperate measures and we have just seen them with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Nicholas Hastings in \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Focus. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or really the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , probably felt it had no choice. The USD's decline against the JPY had got to the point where it was causing not only economic but political damage and something had to be done. By launching what will probably be confirmed as the country's largest ever \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exercise, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has succeeded in pushing the USD back up from just under Y83 to somewhere between Y85-86, where it remains for now. But, JPY bulls should hang on. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 16-09-10 0721GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100916e69g000im\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
