\par\par \b \uc2 INDIAN MORNING BRIEFING: Sensex Likely To be Rangebound\b0\par\par\uc2 1,732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 05:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Energy Service\par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Malaysian markets are closed Thursday for Malaysia Day.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL MARKETS \par DJIA                10572.73  +46.24   +0.44% \par Nasdaq              2301.32   +11.55   +0.50% \par S&P 500             1125.07   +3.97    +0.35% \par FTSE 100            5555.56   -11.85   -0.21% \par Nikkei Stock        9544.81   +28.25   +0.30% \par Hang Seng           21652.73  -72.91   -0.34% \par Kospi               1817.00   -6.88    -0.38% \par SGX Nifty           5844.00   -17.50   -0.29% \par Sept. contract \par  \par USD/JPY             85.72-76     +3.18% \par Range               85.77-82.88 \par EUR/USD             1.3008-11    +0.10% \par Range               1.3036-1.2956 \par  \par CBOT Wheat Dec.     $7.266 per bushel \par Comex Gold          $1,268.70    -$3.00 \par Comex Gold Range    $1,264.50-$1,273.50 \par Nymex Crude (NY)    $76.02       -$0.78 \par  \par  \par CHARTING THE SENSEX \f28 \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's 30-share Sensitive Index is likely to trade in a 19,370-19,620 range, according to charts.\par \par \uc2 A shift out this range would set the tone for the next major move. Above 19,620, the Sensex could rise to major resistance at 19,740, while a drop below 19,370 may trigger a fall to major support at 19,210.\par \par \uc2 The index has to fall below the Sept. 8 intra-day low of 18,540 to indicate a reversal of the short-term uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The National Stock Exchange's 50-share Nifty could be confined to a 5,830-5,885 band.\par \par \uc2 A breakout above 5,885 could lead to a test of major resistance at 5,910, while a fall below 5,830 may push the index down to major support 5,800.\par \par \uc2 The short-term trend would turn bearish on a drop below the Sept. 8 intra-day low of 5,567.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rose Wednesday as encouraging forecasts from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kraft Foods\f28 \uc2 \f2  and McKesson boosted investors' expectations of how the corporate sector is faring in the weak economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft was among the Dow's best performers, up 1.7%. The company, which recently bought confectioner Cadbury, said it expects sales from its chocolate business to jump to $10 billion by 2013, driven by developing markets and added revenue growth from the acquisition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft executives, speaking at a New York analyst meeting, also forecasted growth in its biscuits business and its gum-and-candy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Standard & Poor's 500 index's gains were led by the health-care sector, which was boosted by a jump in McKesson, up 5.4%. The pharmaceutical supplier told investors at a conference that it expects to hit fiscal-year guidance despite slowing health-care volumes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday's activity followed a wave of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yen's rise, marking the first time Japanese authorities publicly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets since 2004. The move sent the dollar sharply higher against the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mixed Thursday though Japanese exporters continued to benefit from a weaker yen after Japanese authorities' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Nikkei Share Average and New Zealand's NZX-50 were up, while Australia's S&P/ASX 200 and South Korea's Kospi Composite were down. Dow Jones Industrial Average futures were 21 points lower in screen trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese exporters were again shining in Tokyo, on relief that authorities had finally taken action to weaken the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Foreign investors' appetite in Japan stocks is also lifting sentiment," said Kazuhiro Takahashi, general manager at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  was up 2.3%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toshiba\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 2.0% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 1.3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Energy firm Inpex shed 0.6% due to weakness in crude oil prices and a ratings downgrade from \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  to neutral from buy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In South Korea, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tong Yang Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst Lee Jae-mahn said "the Kospi a bit tired. Its upward strength has somewhat weakened after recent rises and ahead of the Korean holidays" from Sept. 21 to 23.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  was down 0.3% and KB Financial lost 1.2% but GS Engineering rose 1.9% after it won $628.4 million worth of orders for two Oman projects.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders were watching for signs of follow-up action from Japanese authorities after they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in markets and weakened the yen sharply Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was at Y85.57, from Y85.63 late in New York while the euro was at Y111.17, from Y111.36 and at $1.2986 from $1.3012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold futures pulled back Wednesday as market participants sold holdings to cash in on the metal's record highs and demand declined on a lack of market moving news. Spot gold was at $1,266.70 per troy ounce, down $1.50 from late New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Base metals on the London Metal Exchange closed mostly lower Wednesday, weighed down by weaker-than-expected U.S. data and speculation that China will step up measures to cool its property market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October Nymex crude oil futures were down 29 cents at $75.73 per barrel on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CALENDAR OF EVENTS Sept. 16 \par 0900 IST Bangalore:   Unique Identification Authority of India chairman, \par                       Maruti Suzuki executive at National Association \par                       of Software and Services Companies summit \par 0915 IST New Delhi:   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  Deputy Governor Usha Thorat \par                       at event \par 1030 IST New Delhi:   Commerce and industry minister, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                       executive director for merchant banking, Unitech \par                       managing director at Federation of Indian Chambers \par                       of Commerce and Industry international real estate \par                       summit \par 1200 IST New Delhi:   Weekly inflation data due for week ending Sept. 4 \par 1200 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  mid-quarter monetary policy \par 1230 IST Mumbai:      Ramky Infrastructure executive chairman at \par                       company's initial public offering press meet \par 1930 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hindustan Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  executives at press meet post \par                       annual shareholders' meeting \par N/A:                  Unitech annual shareholders' meeting \par 0700 GMT EU:          European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing council and general \par                       council meeting \par 0830 GMT UK:          August U.K. monthly retail sales figures \par 1230 GMT US:          August producer price index \par 1230 GMT US:          Sept. 11 unemployment insurance weekly claims report \par                       - initial claims \par 1400 GMT US:          Senate Committee on banking, housing, and urban \par                       affairs - U.S. treasury secretary testifies to \par                       senate committee hearing on exchange rate policies \par 1400 GMT US:          Sept. 4 DJ-BTMU U.S. business barometer \par 1800 GMT US:          House committee on ways and means - U.S. treasury \par                       secretary testifies to House committee hearing on \par                       Chinese exchange rate \par 1900 GMT US:          International Monetary Fund publishes millennium \par                       development goals paper \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Dow Jones/WSJ \par =UPDATE: GEITHNER: 'VERY CONCERNED' ABOUT CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's move toward a more flexible exchange rate has been "too slow," Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner will tell U.S. lawmakers Thursday, calling on a more balanced relationship between the two powers. (published 0022 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN: TO TAKE DECISIVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS WHEN NECESSARY -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Thursday that the government will take decisive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steps when necessary, suggesting the authorities would not hesitate to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to tackle the yen's rapid rise, Kyodo News reported. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ GOVERNOR: UNCONVENTIONAL EASING HIGHLY EFFECTIVE VS RECENT FINANCIAL CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Thursday that unconventional monetary easing measures were "highly effective" against the "acute pains" in the recent financial crisis. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RBNZ KEEPS CASH RATE ON HOLD AS RECOVERY SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand Thursday held the Official Cash Rate at 3.00% and highlighted ongoing economic uncertainty, particularly after the 7.0 magnitude earthquake in the country's second-largest city of Christchurch earlier this month. (published 2151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 4TH UPDATE: US FILES WTO CASES VS CHINA ON STEEL, ELECTRONIC PAYMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. filed two new trade cases against China at the World Trade Organization, claiming discrimination against U.S. steel makers and credit-card companies. (published 2253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA ECON PLANNER: CAN 'ABSOLUTELY' MEET 3% CPI TARGET THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic planning agency said late Wednesday the country can "absolutely" meet it target of around a 3% rise in the consumer price index this year, despite the CPI rising 3.5% from a year earlier in August. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CIC EXECUTIVE: INVESTMENT RETURNS TO STAY LOW IN MATURE FIXED-INCOME MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging markets are rising in importance as returns in mature fixed-income markets such as the U.S. and Europe are likely to stay low for five to 10 years, an executive with China's sovereign-wealth fund said Thursday. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HUADIAN SEEKS BUYER FOR 13.65% STAKE IN YANTAI BANK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Huadian Corp., one of China's five major power utilities, is looking to raise funds by selling its 13.65% stake in Yantai Bank Co., the company said in a document filed to the Shanghai United Assets and Equity Exchange. (published 0053 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALINTA ENERGY: RECEIVED ALL TRADE BIDS FOR COMPANY, ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alinta Energy Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday that it has received all trade bids for its whole business and individual assets and will assess them over the coming week. (published 2302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: SPRINT RULES OUT QUICK CLEARWIRE BUYOUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-15-10 2306ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sprint Nextel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is unlikely to buy the remainder of next-generation network operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Clearwire Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (CLWR) or seek control of the company in the near term, as either option would be too expensive, Sprint Chief Financial Officer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert Brust\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Indian Media \par State Bank Of India In Talks With RBI To Form Holding Company - Economic Times \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Sell African Towers To Bharti Infratel Arm - Economic Times \par India Panel To Investigate Bharat Sanchar's Financial Performance - Economic Times \par Vedanta Replies To Show Cause Notices On Orissa Bauxite Project - PTI \par India Mines Bill May Prohibit Sharing Of Mining Leases - Economic Times \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jet Airways\f28 \uc2 \f2  India Unlikely To Get Waiver On External Commercial Borrowing - Business Standard \par Air India To Spin Off Low-Cost Carrier Unit Into Separate Company - Economic Times \par Future Group Set To Buy Shopping Portal Chaupaati Bazaar - Economic Times \par Actis Biologics To Raise $380 Mln Via Sale Of Stakes In India, Malaysia Units - Business Standard \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taisho Pharmaceutical\f28 \uc2 \f2  Also Interested In Buying Out Paras Pharmaceutical - Mint \par India's Lanco Awards Order To China's Harbin At Sharply Reduced Cost - DNA Money \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-15-10 2306ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62500   \par \par \uc2 Dokume