\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-After yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , funds see lower volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss  \par \uc2 893 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 23:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 16 (Reuters) - After Japan's yen-selling effort on Wednesday pushed the unit down 3.0 percent versus the U.S. dollar, investors expect fewer aggressive bets because of ongoing fear of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A day after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold nearly 2 trillion yen ($20.9 billion) to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fund managers are bracing for low volatility and tight trading ranges, even though they expect the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets for some time.\par \par \uc2 Dollar/yen traded nearly flat on Thursday, moving within a 60-basis point range, closing around 85.77. Investors expect days like Thursday to be the norm for the next several months, believing Wednesday's steep fall to be a one-time event.\par \par \uc2 For Thurday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report, click on [ID:nN16164371].\par \par \uc2 Despite the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many still think the yen's recent trend has not necessarily been reversed for good.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think we will see an aggressive weakening in the yen despite the fact that the yen looks overvalued from a valuation perspective," said Thomas Kressin, senior vice president and lead portfolio manager of Pimco's Global Investor Series \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategy Fund in Munich, Germany. The fund has assets under management of about 100 million euros ($130 million).\par \par \uc2 "If you look at past historical turning points in the dollar/yen exchange rate, it has been usually accompanied by a tightening policy by the Federal Reserve that would precipitate outflows from Japan. This is something I cannot see in the forseeable future and so I think the major scenario is one of a trading range from this point going forward," he said.\par \par \uc2 The options market suggests the same thing. Implied volatility on dollar/yen, a gauge of the market's outlook for how sharp movements would be in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair, has fallen on Thursday, reflecting expectations that there would be no major hiccup over the next 30 days to push the spot price wildly in either direction.\par \par \uc2 One-month dollar/yen volatilities <JPY1MO=> slid to 10.95 percent from as high as 13.25 percent on Wednesday. Volatilities surged to 15.75 percent last week as investors started getting nervous about the prospect of a Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And while risk reversals, a measure of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment, show a less upbeat view in the options market, with the level currently at 0.55 volatilities <JPY1MRR=ICAP> from about 1.55 in late August, some investors are biding their time before they reload on long yen trades.\par \par \uc2 WAITING IT OUT\par \par \uc2 "Range trading is the best way to describe the price action in dollar/yen in the next week or two. We'll have to wait and see," said John Taylor, chairman of the New York-based \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts, the world's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedge fund with assets under management of about $8 billion.\par \par \uc2 The fund is not totally out of the short dollar/yen trade despite losing 2.0 percent on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The BoJ will be there for a long time at 83 yen. So it's not clear yet whether we should be completely off the trade," Taylor said. "You have a 2 yen reversal, does that make you give it up when you made a ton of money on the way down? It makes you say, 'I shouldn't be bigger than I was before.'"\par \par \uc2 Others are still debating whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been successful.\par \par \uc2 David Kupersmith, head trader at Third Wave Global Investors, a global macro hedge fund in Greenwich, Connecticut, noted yen movements were tracking the fixed income market but a few weeks ago that relationship failed. In recent weeks, global bond yields had declined in tandem with weakness in dollar/yen.\par \par \uc2 That and the belief yen strength had gone too far prompted them to bet against the yen. As of late Wednesday, Third Wave has made no changes in their positions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, funds that hold a long-term view such as the London-based Pareto Investment Management were bothered little by the three percent fall in the yen. It is keeping its long yen position.\par \par \uc2 Constantine Ponticos, Pareto's head of research, said capital flows still favor a strong yen. Pareto, with assets under management of more than $45 billion, did lose money on Wednesday with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but "considering how much money we've made on this yen move (strengthening), it's not terrible at all," he said.\par \par \uc2 Still, there are those who are continuing to reduce their long bets on the yen.\par \par \uc2 "Prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we thought the probability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was getting higher and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was becoming less undervalued or even moving into overvaluation," said Jonathan Xiong, director and global investment strategist at Mellon Capital Management. Xiong is part of a team that oversees $28.6 billion in assets in San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 "We had already cut our long positions by 40 percent in the earlier part of this month. Our models see more risk in the yen and we may pull back even more on our long positions."\par \par \uc2 (Addition reporting by Nick Olivari and Wanfeng Zhou)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FUNDS|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|UKI|CANT|AUF|J|Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100916e69g001kt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
