\par\par \b \uc2 TREASURIES-Yields inch up, yen moves watched\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Treasury debt yields edge up, curve stays steep\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying seen but not linked to yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Further quantitative easing by Fed expected\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 16 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury yields edged up in Europe on Thursday but the yield curve remained at its steepest in over a month on market talk Japan would buy short-term Treasuries to park the dollars it purchased during its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Market participants were keeping a close eye on signs of further action by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six years on Wednesday sparked buying in two-year Treasuries, taking the 2/10-year Treasury yield curve to its steepest in over a month around 224 basis points.\par \par \uc2 "The Japanese buying story potentially could result in further curve steepening because the Japanese authorities would invest the proceeds of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in short-term Treasuries," said Philip Shaw, an economist at Investec.\par \par \uc2 Trader said they saw some institutional buying out of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  but this was not related to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day to curb yen strength.\par \par \uc2 "They continue to focus on the belly of the curve which has been a trend for the past two months. The market is in OK shape. There's not nearly the concern and choppy price action we saw yesterday," one trader said.\par \par \uc2 Two-year T-notes <US2YT=RR> were yields rose a basis point to 0.49 percent as prices retreated with investors waiting to see if there would be further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 10-year T-note yield <US10YT=R> also edged up about 1 bp to 2.730 percent, keeping the 2/10-year yield gap around 224 bps.\par \par \uc2 Traders see chances of another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing if the dollar slips back below 85 yen, after Japan sold an estimated 2 trillion yen ($23 billion) on Wednesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other central banks around the region keen to retain their export competitiveness has also boosted prices of U.S. Treasuries, although the urgency to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lessened in recent times due to the strength of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of regional giants Japan and China.\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve's next move will also be monitored amid talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may reinstate quantitative easing measures it first adopted it late 2008 to combat the global credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 "The United States is not on a definitive road to recovery so rates are going to stay low for quite some time.. Everyone is looking for quantitative easing," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 The Fed bought $300 billion in Treasuries last year in a move seen aimed at helping lower long-term interest rates to support a slowing economy.\par \par \uc2 Signs of a slowdown re-emerged on Wednesday after a report showed a measure of New York state business conditions slipped to the lowest level in more than a year, while industrial output rose at a slower rate in August. [ID:nN15145257]\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Emelia Sithole-Matarise; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BONDS-TREASURIES|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|NAT|J|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100916e69g000t0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
