\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ data suggests Japan sold Y1.76-1.86 trln Weds\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 11:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan's money market data showed on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day may have totalled around 1.76 trillion to 1.86 trillion yen ($20.52-21.69 billion) .\par \par \uc2 The BOJ's projection for Friday's money market conditions showed there will be 2.26 trillion yen in payments to banks from the public sector.\par \par \uc2 That compared with about 400 billion to 500 billion yen of payments from the government that money brokers had been expecting, excluding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Market players say the 1.76 trillion to 1.86 trillion yen difference between their expectation and the projection is likely a reflection largely of yen payments due to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled two days after the transaction.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time in six years on Wednesday and promised more to come in a bid to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relentless rise from hurting exporters and threatening a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers have estimated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about 2 trillion yen during \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the course of Asian, European and U.S. trade on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, that could be a record for Japanese yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a single day, surpassing selling of 1.666 trillion yen on January 9, 2004.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce on Sept. 30 how much it spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September. ($1=85.75 Yen) (Reporting by Hideyuki Sano and Takaya Yamaguchi; Editing by Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MONEY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|J|G|RBN|ABN|E|U|C|D|M|O|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCO   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100916e69g000l5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
