\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 4-Japan PM says ready to step into  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  markets again\b0\par\par\uc2 907 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  PM signals ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets again\par \par \uc2 * Manufacturing, service-sector sentiment seen worsening\par \par \uc2 * BOJ Tankan recovery may slow, add pressure for BOJ easing\par \par \uc2 * Ruling party backbenchers urge BOJ to ease more\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk seen rising if dlr falls below 85 yen\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Izumi Nakagawa\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Japan's prime minister signalled on Thursday that authorities would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength as sagging manufacturing confidence underscored the threat the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  poses to the fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters monthly poll that tracks the Bank of Japan tankan report showed manufacturing confidence dropped in September from August for the first time in nearly a year as firms struggled with the yen's rise to a 15-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Responding to concerns about the yen's rise, authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets on Wednesday for the first time in six years to knock the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan money market data showed the yen-selling may have totalled up to 1.86 trillion yen ($21.7 billion), which would be a record for a single day.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Naoto Kan, who fended off a leadership challenge from a ruling party powerbroker this week, pointed on Thursday to more yen selling if needed.\par \par \uc2 "If rapid fluctuations in the yen harm Japanese firms' appetite for investing at home and push them to shift their factories overseas, that could further worsen job conditions and affect (our efforts) to overcome deflation," Kan said.\par \par \uc2 "I will take decisive steps if needed from now on as well," he told a business group.\par \par \uc2 Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders believe the likelihood of another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would increase if the dollar slipped back below 85 yen. Its now trading at 85.4 yen, having strengthened from around 83 yen before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PRESSURE ON BOJ?\par \par \uc2 Kan, struggling to unify his party and facing a divided parliament, wants to be proactive in tackling the yen after winning the ruling party leadership race on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He is expected to reshuffle his cabinet soon but retain Yoshihiko Noda as finance minister.\par \par \uc2 "He (Kan) is trying to send a message of his party's solidarity. He is showing the strong intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take decisive action through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ayako Sera, market strategist at \uc2 Sumitomo Trust & Banking\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A panel of junior lawmakers in the ruling Democratic Party of Japan (DPJ) urged the Bank of Japan to call an extraordinary meeting to ease policy and so support the government's efforts.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources have said the authority has no plan to call an emergency meeting but is ready to act at its next scheduled meeting in early October if the economic recovery remains under threat.\par \par \uc2 The panel suggested the BOJ increase its buying of Japanese government bonds, although BOJ Governor Masaaki Shirakawa reiterated his opposition to the idea.\par \par \uc2 "We hardly observe the fact that massive expansions in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  balance sheets result in an increase in inflation in advanced economies," Shirakawa said in a conference speech.\par \par \uc2 Shirakawa told a securities dealers' gathering later on Thursday that the BOJ would take timely action as needed and keep providing ample funds to money markets.\par \par \uc2 In addition, sources familiar with the matter said on Wednesday the BOJ will not drain the money flowing into the economy as a result of the selling, indicating it plans to use the sold yen as a monetary tool to boost liquidity in the economy.\par \par \uc2 YEN THREAT TO EXPORTS\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the dollar more than 3 percent higher on Wednesday, a big move for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced some international criticism for its solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since most advanced economies are grappling with slow growth at home, making exports an economic imperative, Japan's move heightened concerns countries would launch a round of competitive devaluations to support their own exports.\par \par \uc2 U.S. lawmaker Sander Levin, who chairs a congressional committee examining China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, blamed Beijing for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's "deeply disturbing" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Kan faces domestic pressure for more action on the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar has recovered to about 85 yen now after the government and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday, and we want them to continue taking strong action to reverse the yen's strength," Toshiyuki Shiga, chairman of the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association (JAMA), told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 "A dollar of 85 or 90 yen is not a level at which job losses can be prevented in Japan," he added.\par \par \uc2 Japan's economic recovery from the global crisis has faltered with export growth slowing down. Signs the U.S. recovery is also stuttering has added to Tokyo's concerns.\par \par \uc2 Underlining those concerns, the Reuters Tankan survey, which has a 95 percent correlation with the BOJ's closely watched quarterly tankan business sentiment survey, showed the manufacturers' sentiment index fell 5 points from August to plus 17, down for the first time since October 2009.\par \par \uc2 Still, the Reuters index has risen during the July-September quarter, suggesting the BOJ data due on out on Sept. 29 will also show a rise. ($1=85.75 Yen) (Additional reporting by Yoko Nishikawa, Kaori Kaneko, Tetsushi Kajimoto and Yoko Kubota; Writing by Tetsushi Kajimoto and Linda Sieg; Editing by Edmund Klamann, Nathan Layne and Neil Fullick)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (WRAPUP 4)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100916e69g00046\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
