\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen falls against the dollar; euro climbs\b0\par\par\uc2 903 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 02:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen falls vs dollar, investors wary after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Euro at 1-month high vs dollar, yen after Spain auction\par \par \uc2 * Swiss franc weakens broadly after SNB meeting (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The yen fell against the U.S. dollar on Thursday with the Bank of Japan silent after massive yen-selling in the prior session and investors reluctant to place bets in case the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  begins new sales to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro rose to its highest in more than a month against the dollar and the yen after strong demand at a Spanish bond auction reinforced confidence in Europe's economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Japan sold an estimated 1.8 trillion yen ($21.14 billion) for dollars on Wednesday, a record for a single day, to help its exporters and increase money supply to counter deflation. The dollar value represents 3.7 percent of the daily average market turnover in dollar/yen using the last available data from the Bank of International Settlements.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six years knocked the yen from a 15-year high versus the dollar, but the yen's six-month uptrend does not look broken, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "There is talk of 82 being the line in the sand but surprise is the key element for the Bank of Japan," said Samarjit Shankar, managing director of global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at BNY Mellon in Boston. "A low 84 or high 83 may be sufficient for the Bank of Japan to come back in and show the market there is two-way risk."\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Naoto Kan reiterated on Thursday Japan would take decisive steps on yen strength, Jiji news agency reported, while Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said he expected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. For more see [ID:nTKF107009].\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon New York trading, the dollar was up 0.1 percent <JPY=> at 85.83 yen, well up on the low of 82.87 hit on electronic trading platform EBS on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was just off the session high of 85.84 yen on EBS and on Reuters touched hours earlier. At the peak it broke above the 50-day exponential and simple moving averages.\par \par \uc2 The dollar/yen 12- and 26-day moving average convergence divergence was at -0.33 with the nine-day signal line at -0.57 on Thursday which may indicate more gains lie ahead. The MACD was at -0.68 on Tuesday with the signal line at -0.67. The dollar/yen December future was trading at 85.75 yen <JYZ0>.\par \par \uc2 BOJ ON HOLD\par \par \uc2 Traders said there were no signs of yen-selling by Japanese authorities though there were indications some investors were reversing bets on the yen.\par \par \uc2 "We are beginning to see some funds moving in the same direction (as the Bank of Japan), unwinding long yen positions," said Greg Salvaggio, vice president of trading at Tempus Consulting in Washington. He added investors should look out for stops at 86.10 yen.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the dollar's upside may be capped around 85.83 yen, where a trendline from the dollar's highs in May and June falls.\par \par \uc2 Others said Japanese authorities may have a hard time fighting the yen's strength, given narrow yield spreads between Japanese and U.S. government bonds.\par \par \uc2 "It is almost inevitable that the Japanese authorities will have to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  heading into year end with dollar/yen likely to remain under downward pressure as the U.S. economy slows and the Fed moves towards renewed monetary easing," said Lee Hardman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 The Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Traders said Japanese exporters want to sell the dollar above 85 yen before half-year book-closings at month end.\par \par \uc2 SPANISH BOND SALE\par \par \uc2 The euro <EUR=> rallied 0.6 percent to $1.3078 after rising to $1.3117 according to Reuters data, its highest since Aug. 11, after auctions of 10- and 30-year Spanish government bonds produced lower yields than the sale in June. [ID:nLDE68F0QX]\par \par \uc2 Traders in London said the euro's initial rise after the results took out stop-loss orders placed around $1.3047, the 61.8 percent retracement of its sell-off in August.\par \par \uc2 It rose as high as 112.40 yen <EURJPY=>, also its highest in about a month and adding to gains after dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove it up roughly 3 percent on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc weakened broadly after the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  kept interest rates unchanged as expected and said that it expected a slowdown in economic growth due to strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nWEA8411]\par \par \uc2 The euro jumped 1.7 percent to 1.3273 francs <EURCHF=>, the biggest daily rise since May 19. The U.S. dollar gained 1.1 percent to 1.0146 francs <CHF=>. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ For dollar/yen correlations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/wyn43p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/wyn43p}}}\uc2  For PDF on the yen's rise {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/zuz33p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/zuz33p}}}\uc2  For graphic on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/wym42p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/wym42p}}}\uc2  For Insider on yen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/rak63p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/rak63p}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ (Reporting by Nick Olivari and Wanfeng Zhou; Additional reporting by Vivianne Rodrigues and Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss in New York and Neal Armstrong in London; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 10)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|UKI|CANT|AUF|J|Z|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100916e69g0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
