\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,030 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: GEITHNER: 'VERY CONCERNED' ABOUT CHINA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's move toward a more flexible exchange rate has been "too slow," Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner will tell U.S. lawmakers Thursday, calling on a more balanced relationship between the two powers. (published 0022 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA YUAN HITS NEW HIGH AHEAD OF GEITHNER TESTIMONY, IGNORES DOLLAR STRENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan hit another high against the U.S. dollar Thursday, ignoring the dollar's recent sharp rebound, in a sign of Beijing's accommodative stance before U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner testifies at a key Congressional hearing on China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: BOJ LEAVES SOME \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS IN MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  skipped its Thursday morning money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , refraining--as expected--from draining any funds from the market, in a sign that it's not at this point sterilizing the yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the government that moved aggressively Wednesday to weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF OFFICIAL: WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WHEN APPROPRIATE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market when deemed necessary, a finance ministry official said Thursday. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA'S LOWE: ECONOMY MORE EXPOSED THAN EVER TO CHINA SWINGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy is more exposed than ever to the vagaries of Chinese economic growth, and little can be done to guard against the uncertainties, Phil Lowe, Assistant Governor at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: RBNZ KEEPS CASH RATE ON HOLD AS RECOVERY SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand Thursday held the Official Cash Rate at 3.00% and highlighted ongoing economic uncertainty, particularly after the 7.0 magnitude earthquake in the country's second-largest city of Christchurch earlier this month. (published 2151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEXT NEW ZEALAND RATE HIKE TO COME IN MARCH - POLL OF ECONOMISTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists are now tipping the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to raise the Official Cash Rate at its March rate review, according to a snap poll Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held the policy rate at 3.00% and surprised markets with its dovish tone. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA BUSINESS CONFIDENCE SLUMPS IN 3Q - WESTPAC-ACCI SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business confidence fell in the third quarter of 2010 compared with the previous quarter, a private sector survey showed Thursday. (published 0123 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA CONSUMER INFLATION EXPECTATIONS 3.1% IN SEPTEMBER VS 2.8% IN AUGUST-MI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian consumer inflationary expectations rose slightly in September after five straight months of declines, according to an industry survey published Thursday. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA EXPECTS KRW175 TLN TAX REVENUE 2010, KRW187.8 TLN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea raised its tax revenue forecast for this year as the domestic economy's recovery has boosted consumption and hence tax collection, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAILAND KEEPS 2010 EXPORT GROWTH TARGET BUT FLAGS STRONG BAHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's full-year export growth target remains intact at 20%, despite the baht's sharp rise against the U.S. dollar, Commerce Ministry Permanent Secretary Yanyong Phuangrach said Thursday. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI AUGUST INDUSTRIAL SENTIMENT TURNS DOWN ON BAHT WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial sentiment index turned lower in August, after rising for two straight months, as corporate executives became worried about the baht's strength, rising interest rates, and the likely economic slowdown in the second half. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY FLAT IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's manufacturing activity was flat in August after a steady expansion in the first half of the year, data released Thursday showed. (published 2306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA ECON PLANNER: CAN 'ABSOLUTELY' MEET 3% CPI TARGET THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic planning agency said late Wednesday the country can "absolutely" meet it target of around a 3% rise in the consumer price index this year, despite the CPI rising 3.5% from a year earlier in August. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JIMI LIKELY TO REMAIN JAPAN FINANCIAL SERVICES MINISTER - NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan is likely to keep Financial Services Minister Shozaburo Jimi in his post, the Nikkei reported in its Thursday evening edition. (published 0312 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHIEF OF AUDIT AGENCY KIM HWANG-SIK NAMED PRIME MINISTER - YONHAP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kim Hwang-sik, head of the South Korean Board of Audit and Inspection, has been picked as the new prime minister, Yonhap news agency reported Thursday, citing unidentified presidential officials. (published 0205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN REGULATOR: BANKS' CAPITAL POSITION STRENGTHENED IN PAST 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The capital position of Taiwan's domestic banks strengthened over the past two years and the lenders should be able to withstand a crisis similar to 2008's global financial crisis, the island's banking regulator said Wednesday. (published 0112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CIC EXECUTIVE: INVESTMENT RETURNS TO STAY LOW IN MATURE FIXED-INCOME MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging markets are rising in importance as returns in mature fixed-income markets such as the U.S. and Europe are likely to stay low for five to 10 years, an executive with China's sovereign-wealth fund said Thursday. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA GOVERNMENT A$1.25B SEP 2030 INDEXED BONDS PRICE AT 2.66% REAL YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government said Thursday it has sold A$1.25 billion in 2.5% Sept. 20, 2030 Treasury-indexed bonds to the public. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAY RAISE, NOT CUT, PRESSURE FOR YUAN ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the surface, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may appear to have temporarily frustrated international efforts to leverage faster \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform in China. (published 2208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: JAPANESE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WILL LIKELY HAVE A SEQUEL \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's "shock and awe" overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets has been effective, but it's almost certain to be repeated to ensure efforts to slow the yen's appreciation are successful. (published 1829 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BIG PICTURE: FACTORY DATA ARE DISAPPOINTING BUT NOT DISASTER \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to cool off the sizzling yen highlights a strategy being employed worldwide: nations are pinning their hopes that manufacturing--especially exportable goods--will lead to stronger growth. (published 1737 GMT) [ 16-09-10 0400GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100916e69g0007l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
